{PARA 19 "" 0 "" {TEXT 286 14 "Anonymous" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 
"" {TEXT 214 11 " Problem 1." }{TEXT 287 3 "   " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 287 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 287 44 "Generate 8 random 3 by \+
3 matrices using the " }{TEXT 215 12 "RandomMatrix" }{TEXT 287 19 " co
mmand from the  " }{TEXT 216 13 "LinearAlgebra" }{TEXT 287 42 " packag
e. As each matrix is generated use " }{TEXT 217 11 "Eigenvalues" }
{TEXT 287 160 " to compute its eigenvalues. Then take the product of t
he eigenvalues, and check that for each matrix, this product is equal \+
to the determinant of the matrix.  " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 287 0 "" 
}}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 287 1 "[" }{TEXT 218 6 "Hint: " }{TEXT 287 79 
"The product will be complicated algebraically and you will need to ap
ply first " }{TEXT 219 6 "expand" }{TEXT 287 7 ", then " }{TEXT 220 8 
"simplify" }{TEXT 287 132 " to reduce the product of the eigenvalues t
o an integer. First try to do for a single matrix , then make a loop t
o do it 8 times.]  " }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 8 "resta
rt:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 20 "with(LinearAlgebra);
